<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further evaluate <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CurDKV</span> and <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AdaCurDKV</span> on the Ruler benchmark, focusing on needle-in-a-haystack (NIAH) subtasks, which measure a model’s ability to recover rare, high-salience facts embedded in long distractor contexts. These tasks are particularly sensitive to the retention of semantically critical key-value tokens. Full cache results are highlighted in Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3 Results on Ruler ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ Value-Guided KV Compression for LLMs via Approximated CUR Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>KV compression methods on needle-in-a-haystack tasks for Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct and Mistral-7B-Instruct (
<span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-caret-square-down" aria-hidden="true">
</span>: compression ratio). Friedman statistic of 25.6/21.7 (for 30% compression) and 12.3 (for 90% compression) with p-values <math id="S4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math> indicate the statistical significance of the result obtained by <span id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CurDKV</span>  over the baselines. Full results for other compression ratios are highlighted in Tables <a href="#A3.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Value-Guided KV Compression for LLMs via Approximated CUR Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> and <a href="#A3.T16" title="Table 16 ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Value-Guided KV Compression for LLMs via Approximated CUR Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> of Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Value-Guided KV Compression for LLMs via Approximated CUR Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. Each result cell “<math id="S4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x/y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x/y</annotation></semantics></math>” indicate accuracies with LLaMA/Mistral.</figcaption>
